Package: RegCompassR
Title: Multiome Regulatory Evidence and Metabolic Reaction Analysis
Version: 2.4.12
Authors@R: c(person(given = "RegCompass", family = "Developers", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "dev@example.com"))
Author: RegCompass Developers [aut, cre]
Maintainer: RegCompass Developers <dev@example.com>
Description: Integrates paired single-cell RNA and ATAC regulatory evidence
    with genome-scale metabolic reaction analysis. Stage 1 applies a configurable
    min_cells threshold before normalization, with a default of 500, and passes
    the same retained cell set to downstream metacell construction. Stage 2 uses
    a configurable min_cells_per_stratum threshold that also defaults to 500.
    Routing is resolved independently for every broad cell type. A cell type
    with at least two retained conditions uses the common-dictionary Pando
    condition-GRN procedure: candidate edges are discovered on the complete cell
    type and separately in every retained condition, exact TF-peak-target triples
    are unioned into one frozen dictionary, and every condition is refitted with
    the same unscaled Gaussian identity Pando interaction model. Only estimable
    coefficients with BH-adjusted P below 0.05 from target fits whose fit_status
    is exactly ok enter the condition regulatory penalty; rank-deficient target
    fits remain auditable but contribute zero regulatory penalty. A cell type
    with one retained condition uses the original standard Pando GRN and creates
    no condition coefficient. Standard Pando uses the configured fixed tf_cor
    and peak_cor candidate thresholds without cell-count-dependent adjustment.
    RegCompass owns the parallel scheduler. Condition-mode Pando objects are
    initialized independently by broad cell type, pooled and condition-by-cell-
    type candidate-discovery tasks run within the single worker budget, exact
    dictionaries are frozen at a strict cell-type barrier, and condition-by-cell-
    type fixed-dictionary GLMs are then dispatched with nested Pando target
    parallelism disabled. Different cell types retain their own Pando objects and
    local peak/motif feature spaces. Standard Pando is parallelized only across
    independent broad cell types. TF and ATAC values are separately averaged
    over exact SuperCell membership before regulatory multiplication. Metacells use one multimodal
    WNN graph per broad cell type and remain condition-pure after membership
    splitting. Optional raw ATAC fragment files are aggregated to final metacell
    barcodes and recounted before metacell TF-IDF. RNA support, regulatory
    effects, GPR rules, cell-type-specific union GEM construction and directional
    penalties use consistent reaction ordering, bounds and medium scenarios.
    Stage 5 uses the original MATLAB CORDA2 algorithm from
    schultzdre/Constraint-Based-Modeling/CORDA2.m as the default context-specific
    completion after mapping cell-type multiome evidence to HC, MC, NC and OT
    reactions. FASTCORE and complete full-GEM scoring remain explicit
    supplementary routes. The adjustable original controls are MCxNCthresh,
    constraint, constrainby, om and ci under corda2_args. Actively reversible
    reactions are split once, the opposite directional copy is closed during each
    target assessment, and the original Step 1, Step 2.1, Step 2.2 and Step 3
    dependency transitions are preserved. With parallel Layer 2 execution,
    directional targets are parallelized only within the current CORDA2 step, all
    results are reduced in original directional order at a strict step barrier,
    and the step-local worker pool is released before the next step begins.
    Cell-type-by-medium models remain independent and are reused by primary and
    RNA-only scoring.
